**Quote from WHK Control Philosophy**:
"This uniform mode structure aligns with ISA-106 state-based control concepts and ISA-88 equipment phases, where every phase has the same set of possible states."

**Best Practice**: Implement state machines FIRST, before detailed sequence logic. States provide the framework; phases/steps fill in the details. Standardized states enable both operational consistency AND powerful data analytics.
